# Copy to .env only if it does not exist. Use your own credentials; never commit .env.
# The cached demo needs no keys. See docs/ZHANG_HAO_HANDOFF.md for each run mode.
# Live instruments and the OpenGWAS index rebuild require this token:
OPENGWAS_JWT=
# Optional Slack deployment: operator's installed bot and app-level tokens.
# Ordinary users of the deployed bot do not supply these:
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
SLACK_APP_TOKEN=
# Optional LLM keys, for LOCAL single-user development only. Each belongs to one
# service: a key for one provider cannot authenticate another. The llm/ layer takes a
# credential per request and never reads these; only the unfinished agent.py template
# still reads GEMINI_API_KEY from the environment.
# In a hosted deployment the user supplies their own key per session and it is NOT
# stored - see HANDOFF_1F.md. Leave these blank unless you are running locally.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Reserved optional variable; no current code reads it:
S2_API_KEY=
# These variables configure one local process. A shared BYOK interface is not yet implemented.
